WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.010
Doll Festival!

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.550
It's begun getting warm recently.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.330
Yeah.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.400
And because of that, I can't get up in 
the morning and it's really annoying.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.760
You sleep all year. 
You know that, right?

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:53.050
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho...

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.340
Heave-ho.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.570
I wonder what they're doing.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.180
Open it up!

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.110
Okay!

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.020
Ready... go!

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.620
I wonder what's about to start?

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.120
Oh, I know.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.170
I've seen this on TV before.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.620
TV?

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.580
You know...

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.460
Mr. Panda, could I 
get your autograph?!

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.920
Mr. Panda, could I 
shake your hand?!

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.590
Mr. Panda! Mr. Panda! 
Autograph! Autograph!

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.480
So cool! Hand shake! Hand shake!

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.890
Mr. Panda! So cooly cute!

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:49.300
Could you not feature me 
in your incorrect delusions?

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:50.730
String!

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.550
Okay!

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.990
Oh, it's the Doll Festival.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:02:59.650
What?

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.110
The Doll Festival <i>(Hina Matsuri)</i>?

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.880
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.480
That would be a summer 
festival <i>(natsu matsuri)</i>.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.700
That would be blind stitching 
<i>(matsuri nui)</i>.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:12.620
There!

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.290
That would be fishing<i>(tsuri)</i>.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.660
The Doll Fes-ti-val!

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.430
The festival for girls where they 
put up dolls as decorations.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:24.530
Oh, I know that one.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.930
The bamboo leaf cakes are delicious.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.780
I think you eat those on 
Children's Day, actually.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.320
You have a younger sister, don't you?

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.770
You don't remember the festival?

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:40.690
Oh, it's the day that you eat 
the hard and soft ones.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.910
Are you only able
 to remember food, by chance?

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.850
Heave-ho, heave-ho...

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.220
Hey.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.230
You should set them up like this.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.780
See? All done!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.510
Where'd you even get that?!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.560
I thought this might happen, so...

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.470
Penguin & Miss Penko Figures

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.550
Please don't use memories 
I want to forget as decorations...

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.850
And this is the Doll Festival!

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.980
It's a festival full 
of ancient tradition!

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.860
Then I'll help put up 
the decorations, too.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:23.820
Clay dolls?

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.690
That might be a bit too ancient...

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.510
Do you display clay dolls 
at your house, Miss Sasako?

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.830
No... I'm sorry.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.330
All right, my turn.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.500
I have nothing but bad 
feelings about this.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.330
What is this?

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:44.160
The three ladies in waiting <i>(sannin kanjo)</i>.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.220
Those are sweet potatoes <i>(kansho)</i>!

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.560
Five trees?

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.560
Five-Tree Grove <i>(go-hon bayashi)</i>

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.310
Are they supposed to be the 
five court musicians <i>(go-nin bayashi)</i>?

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:54.590
Correct!

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.400
Uh, that's pushing it quite a bit.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:58.860
In the way!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.860
In the way!

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.990
They said you're in the 
way, Mr. Penguin.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.000
<i>You</i> are the one who was 
getting in their way!

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.580
At this rate, they're never 
going to finish decorating.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.000
I guess there's no choice 
but to do this seriously.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.780
Hey, Polar Bear!

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.920
You're trying to wake
 me up, aren't you?!

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.510
Oh, Grizzly.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.220
Good guess.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.050
You're always getting in 
the way of my sleep.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:39.060
Now I'm getting to know the timing 
that you'll call me, damn it.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.770
Have you given up being 
a shut-in <i>(hikikomori)</i>?

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.150
I'm holed up for the winter <i>(fuyugomori)</i>!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:49.010
Damn it, waking me up 
whenever you get a chance.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.920
How many times do you think 
you woke me up this winter?

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.920
Now thanks to you, 
I'm completely awake.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.080
Well, that's good.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.380
No, it's not!

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.990
Sure it is. Look.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:03.980
The Doll Festival, huh?

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:07.970
What the...

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.440
Why are there clay dolls 
and potatoes on there?!

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.510
Could you help them 
out a bit, Grizzly?

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:16.020
Jeez... Hey, let me have that.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.200
Eat?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.370
No, I'm not gonna eat it!

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.730
See? You put it here.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.690
All right, here we go!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.220
Next!

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.030
Here.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.770
Don't hand me weird things!

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.040
Heave-ho, heave-ho...

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:38.480
Jeez...

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.860
So, this goes here...

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:43.970
Got it?

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.000
Thanks!

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.390
It's finished!

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.290
There. It's perfect.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.420
It's done, it's done!

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.060
Done...

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.490
How's that, Polar Bear?

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.280
That's amazing!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.280
Not bad.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.680
But it's blocking the entrance.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:14.240
Wha?

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:20.060
It's perfectly in the way.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:24.870
You always do go a bit 
too far, Grizzly.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:27.210
<i>You</i> are the one that told me to do it!

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:31.220
By the way, who's celebrating this?

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.090
Huh? What do you mean?

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:37.420
The Doll Festival, is a day to celebrate girls.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.430
Who are the girls here?

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:40.970
Oh...

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.400
And who are the boys?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:44.440
Here.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.020
Here.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.280
So all of you are guys?!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.320
Damn it, why the hell are you celebrating 
the Doll Festival <i>(Hina Matsuri)</i>?!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:54.610
I think it's okay.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.780
I mean, they're all baby chicks <i>(hina)</i>.

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:00.750
Oh, I get it.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.390
The Doll Festival <i>(Hina Matsuri)</i> is for them
since they're baby chicks <i>(hina)</i>.

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:05.630
Hey! That makes no sense!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.130
He totally went with it.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.710
He's in a better mood
after his hibernation.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.510
Are there any girls here? Anybody?

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.640
Well, there's Miss Sasako.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.800
Huh? Who, me?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.520
U-Um...

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:29.950
You got a problem with this?

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:30.810
No...

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.860
But it's a festival for girls...

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:38.670
Let's not complicate 
things further, Miss Sasako.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:39.900
Don't worry.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:43.060
Lately they talk about girl power, 
no matter how old you are.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.430
You're somehow making this even 
more difficult, Polar Bear.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:50.980
Hey, you're not going to wear 
a kimono, Miss Sasako?

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:53.670
What? I didn't bring 
anything like that.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.000
Leave the kimono to me.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:04.590
What do you think?

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:07.650
No one asked you
 to put on a kimono!

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.880
Wow, you look so cute, Miss Sasako!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.090
Thank you.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:24.900
Huh?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.890
Hey, could I ask you a 
question, Miss Sasako?

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:30.290
What is it, Panda?

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.760
Are you married, Miss Sasako?

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:34.870
Huh?!

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:41.230
Well, you see, Panda... 
Before she started working here...

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.180
I am not!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.510
So you're not married.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.570
You can't find anyone?

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.190
Well, something like that.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.870
Then what do you think about 
Mr. Handa, Miss Sasako?

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.600
Huh? Mr. Handa?

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.410
Come on! Tell us!

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.340
How 'bout it?

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.160
Well...

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:01.360
Um...

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:05.040
He's always drinking coffee, isn't he?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.130
Well, I guess that's true.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:11.670
Well, the coffee here is delicious.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.670
It must be because he doesn't 
get paid much at the zoo.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.650
I don't think that's the 
issue here, Panda.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.600
I've always wondered about that.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.540
And he doesn't get that 
much time off, either.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.560
But you take most of the year off.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.830
All aboard!

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:28.020
Huh?

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:29.850
Aboard.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:30.790
Huh?

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:38.860
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.900
We've arrived!

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.460
Arrived...

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.330
A-Arrived...

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.500
Oh, Mr. Handa.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:04.430
<i>M-Miss Sasako looks so cute...</i>

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:06.150
Welcome.

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:07.910
Hold it.

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:09.440
Don't worry about it today. Just sit.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:10.850
But...

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.580
It's the Doll Festival. 
I'll give you a hand.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.210
Could you take this out, Grizzly?

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:18.600
Not wasting any time, are you?!

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.000
Wow!

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.120
It's the Doll Festival, 
so I tried making it.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.670
Hishi mochi?

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:26.620
Yup.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.010
It looks delicious!

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.400
Can I eat it?

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.930
Hold it right there.

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:31.500
Come on.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.010
Oh, right.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.000
Well then, everyone...

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:39.260
Happy Doll Festival!

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:43.970
Happy Doll Festival!

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.970
Thank you for the food!

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:52.700
It's good!

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.560
Good...

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:58.530
Um, Miss Sasako, about earlier...

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:00.560
What is it?

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:02.460
Oh, uh...

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:04.560
Y-You look very nice in a kimono.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.340
Thank you very much.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.710
It's delicious.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:26.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:31.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.670
The Animal Doctor.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.260
Influenza

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.260
Caution

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.720
Mr. Polar Bear, please come this way.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.090
Yes.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.700
Pardon me.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.860
What brings you here today?

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:29.700
How are you feeling?

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:36.260
I've had a fever... 
since this morning.

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.940
You're quite large, Mr. Patient.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:50.580
I'm sorry.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:53.940
I'm going to use the stethoscope, 
so please remove your coat.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:55.640
I'm not wearing one.

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.150
I see...

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.810
Um... I can't reach, so may I climb up?

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.610
You're going to climb on me?

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:07.070
I'm very good at climbing.

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:08.970
On your patients?

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.490
No... I'm good at climbing trees.

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:16.440
I see.

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:31.180
All right, that's good.

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:34.240
You've got a cold.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.030
I'll give you some medicine,

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:38.100
so please stay in bed 
and get some rest.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.730
Pre                          Payment

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:40.850
Prescri                          ment

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:40.980
Prescripti                           nt

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:41.100
Prescriptions

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:41.270
Prescriptions   -

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:41.600
Prescriptions   -      Paym

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:44.360
Prescriptions   -      Payment

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.530
Please take care.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:48.450
Excuse me, may I order?

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.640
Yes, coming right away!

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:01.790
Pardon the intrusion.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.330
What brings you two here?

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:07.920
We came to visit you.

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:10.800
Visit <i>(omimai)</i>?

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.820
That would be twinsies <i>(oniai)</i>.

00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:17.060
That would be an arranged 
meeting <i>(omiai)</i>.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:23.460
Let's hold off on the puns 
while you're sick, Polar Bear?

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.920
Yeah, I'll do that.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.800
You've got quite a fever.

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:33.860
I took some medicine, so I think 
it'll be going down soon.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.620
Is there anything you want 
us to do, Polar Bear?

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:40.600
Nope, I can't think of anything.

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:41.650
Really?

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.580
You're sweating quite a bit.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.080
Then we'll wipe it off for you.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:54.920
How'd you know I was 
out with a fever?

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:57.110
Miss Sasako told us.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.210
That's a lot of sweat.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:05.860
Thanks. I'm feeling better.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.830
You haven't eaten anything since this 
morning, have you, Polar Bear?

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:10.750
I haven't.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.170
Then we'll make you something to eat.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.330
I didn't know you could 
actually do anything

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.950
other than drink café 
mocha, Mr. Penguin.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:24.530
And I think you should learn something 
other than how to laze around.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:28.150
But I'm cute, so that's all I need.

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:31.800
I see. Let's see... 
Where were the pots?

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.430
Oh, I think this is it.

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:37.280
Almost...

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.600
I-I wonder if they're okay...

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:50.330
Could I place my order?

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:51.160
Yes, sir.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.920
Could I get another coffee?

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:53.400
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:59.350
That really startled me.

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:01.400
Who knew it'd rain pots?

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:04.120
It startled me even more. Panda...

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.550
Get off of me. You're heavy.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.580
There aren't enough ingredients to make anything.

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:16.840
What were you thinking about making?

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:22.470
A Sicilian seafood curry with 
plenty of bouillabaisse

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:24.270
that's been simmering for 48 hours.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:28.080
I saw it on a cooking show yesterday 
and it looked really good.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:32.360
I think he might recover 
before that finishes.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:37.240
Well, I can't make it anyway since 
there aren't enough ingredients.

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:39.910
Can't you make something else?

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:43.850
Hey, can't you make anything else?

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.050
I-I can...

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:53.550
Whatcha looking for?

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:54.720
A cook book.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:57.010
You don't know how to make something?

00:17:57.010 --> 00:18:01.620
Chopped Burdock 
Root

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:58.600
I do.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.270
I was just looking through to see if

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:02.160
I could get any ideas of what to make.

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:07.190
Stewed Potatoes

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.650
Hey, what about this book?

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:13.080
Wow, look at this, Mr. Penguin!

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:13.940
What is it?

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:15.970
Oh, it's an album.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:19.000
Look! They're pictures 
of Polar Bear and

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.000
Mr. Grizzly when they were little.

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:28.540
So I guess even those guys 
were cute at one point.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:34.550
I'll put in one of my pictures 
to fit in with the cuteness.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:39.900
Let's not confuse people's 
precious memories, Panda.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:45.030
Hey! I'm in these pictures!

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:47.850
Hey, wasn't I there, too?

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:49.870
Let's see...

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.900
See? You're right here.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:54.810
I'm cut in half!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.580
Aren't there any other pictures?

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:06.060
You're a natural-born 
extra, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:08.000
I'm the star at times, too!

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:09.580
I know!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:14.680
If we show these to Polar 
Bear, it'll make him happy.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.000
I don't think it will.

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:21.900
Polar Bear!

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:22.990
Huh?

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.380
He's asleep.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:27.960
You're right.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.160
I think I'll sleep, too.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:37.580
You're too much of a free spirit, no?

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:44.780
Polar Bear still has a fever.

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:20.780
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:27.070
Hey, I'm coming in.

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:31.460
I heard you had a fever, 
so I came by to make yo—

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.510
The hell are you two doing?

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:39.270
Oh, hello.

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:40.600
Good morning.

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:43.630
Hey, what's wrong?

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:47.330
Hey, you're hot!

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.440
You've got a fever.

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:51.310
Really?

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.640
You, too, Penguin. Ya idiot.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.830
Sorry...

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:57.060
Hurry up...

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:58.440
And get to bed!

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:06.400
Just lay there.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.450
Okay.

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:19.280
Mr. Grizzly, I've closed up the café.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:21.890
Is there anything I can help you with?

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:25.040
All right. I'll have you peel 
some apples for me then.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:25.740
Sure.

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:40.540
It smells really good.

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.720
Nothing less from Grizzly.

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:47.820
Hey, sorry, Polar Bear...

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:53.200
We came by to visit you, but ended 
up causing you trouble instead.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:57.250
It's all right.

00:21:58.070 --> 00:21:59.320
Don't worry about it.

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:14.790
<i>Thank you...</i>

00:22:17.590 --> 00:22:18.780
<i>Everyone.</i>

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:25.780
Next Time

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:58.440
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:58.440 --> 00:23:59.620
What is it, Panda?

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:02.540
Could you introduce me to Bill Gates?

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:04.790
Can't say I have him 
in my address book.

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:07.320
I'd like him to create a 
program where I get paid

00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:09.510
every time I eat bamboo grass.

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:11.630
I can't say I have any idea 
what you're talking about.

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:13.430
Please do your best, Mr. Penguin!

00:24:13.430 --> 00:24:16.510
I'd rather not try my best 
if I don't have to.

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:18.220
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:19.890
Next Week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:22.560
will be presented sneakily, 
so no one finds out.

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.000
South Pole Squad Penguinger
Even More, What is Roasting!?

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:23.510
Let's do it up front.

00:24:23.510 --> 00:24:24.000
Enjoy!
